{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542137-clan-novel-ravnos-or-khalil-is-the-frigging-worst","id":1542137,"title":"Clan Novel Ravnos or \"Khalil is the frigging worst.\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-14T15:06:37-07:00","id":1542137,"title":"Clan Novel Ravnos or \"Khalil is the frigging worst.\"","content":"<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/beforewegoblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Clan-Novel-Ravnos.jpg?resize=169%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i0.wp.com/beforewegoblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Clan-Novel-Ravnos.jpg?resize=169%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i0.wp.com/beforewegoblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Clan-Novel-Ravnos.jpg?resize=169%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> CLAN NOVEL: RAVNOS is the eighth novel in the Clan Novel series for the Vampire: The Masquerade line of tabletop RPGs. I\u2019ve been re-reading the series for the past couple of years and enjoying the world of conspiracies, action, and interlocking plotlines. The series is not without its flaws and wildly changes tones as well as themes depending on the characters. However, it is still something that I think to be quite fun. I also note that the twelve book series has its own smaller series within the books, effectively following authors continuing their own stories when they do two or more books. In this case, Ravnos is a sequel to the Setite novel.<br /> <br /> The premise is that Hesha Ruhadze, Follower of Set high priest, has managed to finally acquire the Eye of Hazimel. The Eye is effectively the One Ring of Sauron (or Eye of Vecna) in that it bestows fantastic powers to its wielder but eventually warps your mind into a parody of itself. It also attracts the attention of Hazimel himself, who is restricted to using Khail Ravana as a minion in order to retrieve it. Khail finds himself stumbling on the erstwhile childe of Hesha, Elizabeth Dimitrios, and the Gangrel Ramona, who all have their own stake in the quest.<br /> <br /> The biggest flaw of this novel is Khalil Ravana himself. He is, deliberately, a complete scumbag. He\u2019s a thieving, scheming, snivelling, cowardly irredeemable piece of ****. You can be a bad person as well as a protagonist in Vampire: The Masquerade, it\u2019s almost mandatory, but Khalil is closer to Gollum rather than, say, Saruman. This is a book written by a woman but there\u2019s a scene where Khalil waits in a woman\u2019s apartment, watches her undress, then forcibly restrains her before draining her dry in a scene deliberately meant to remind you of what it does.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the fact that Khalil gets away with so much awful evil crap is something that makes the book a chore. Vampire novels almost inevitably work best when their condition is a curse and Khalil doesn\u2019t have enough self-awareness to be cursed by it. He\u2019s a living argument for why Paths of Enlightenment aren\u2019t really appropriate for a vampire game or, at least, would be if he cared enough about the Path of Paradox to be anything more than \u201cthe path of what I was going to do anyway.\u201d Indeed, the best part of Khalil\u2019s story is when he chides Ramona for racism against Romani people, saying, yes, HE is a murderous thief but that\u2019s just him. His family is rightfully ashamed of him.<br /> <br /> The best parts of the books are Hesha, Ramona, and Elizabeth\u2019s sections. Hesha may be every bit as evil as Khalil, being a literal priest of a god of evil (which Set wasn\u2019t in RL but is in V:TM) but he has far more depth as a person. Ramona is a vampire who wants to be \u201cgood\u201d but is rather easily led astray by Khalil\u2019s transparent lies. Elizabeth seems to have fallen in from another genre of horror entirely and is as terrified of Khalil as she is of Hesha despite the former being more Buffy vampire than Dracula in terms of intelligence.<br /> <br /> If it sounds like I\u2019m insulting the book, I\u2019m not, well, not entirely. None of this is due to bad writing. Kathleen Ryan is fully capable of writing fantastic vampire fiction. I know, because she\u2019s the author of Setite and that\u2019s one of my favorite V:TM books. However, the protagonist is someone she tries to contrast against all of the others and he\u2019s just not a great place to be in the headspace of. Despite this, I found myself still interested in the plotline between them. The Eye of Hazimel is the most D&amp;D-like artifact in V:TM but it\u2019s very strangeness is one of the reasons the plot works. No one else really looks for magical artifacts in the setting, so the one-eyed man is king.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T19:28:48-07:00","id":1542158,"title":"","content":"It's good that Kali Ravana hasn't been brought back into the new setting at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T12:55:29-07:00","id":1542196,"title":"","content":"Maybe we will see more interesting and more developed Charltans that will make people forget about Khali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T14:01:56-07:00","id":1542198,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest disappointment with the book is how Elizabeth doesn't get to really do anything. She's chained to a pipe for most of the book, and only gets a little to do (or to deal with, because of Khalil's shit and her own newly born vampirism).<br /> <br /> I would love to have seen her exercise more agency. Maybe have more scenes of her trying to come to terms with being an undead creature with a thirst for blood. If for no other reason than, even more than Ramona, Elizabeth is the big fish out of water here. At least Ramona has had time to become used to her body and her needs. Elizabeth is very fresh, which might have permitted us a unique perspective to contrast Khalil.<br /> <br /> At the very least, it would give the reader a break from living in Khalil's head the whole time.<br /> <br /> I really hope Elizabeth went on to bigger and better things. (Maybe she became the first Setite to join the Children of Osiris? That would be neat.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","va